-- title:
--   Raw and probed restart scans over stage indices
-- statement:
--   Fix natural $n,r$, Boolean query functions, a tape, schedule $s$, and learned rational tables. Let $J$ be a finite list of natural stage indices and $A$ an accumulator consisting of an optional restart cursor and a natural attempt tally. Define
--   $$\operatorname{rawRestartScan}(J,A)=\operatorname{foldl}\bigl((A,i)\mapsto\operatorname{countedStage}_i(A),A,J\bigr).$$
--   For a selected ordinal $\ell$ and draw index $a\in\{0,1,2\}$, the probed version carries an additional optional pair $D$ of natural numbers for a draw start and denominator and folds the probed stages:
--   $$\operatorname{probedRestartScan}_{\ell,a}(J,(A,D))=\operatorname{foldl}(\operatorname{probedStage}_{\ell,a},(A,D),J).$$
--   These definitions use each list entry as its stage index and extract the value of the charged fold. Arbitrary initial accumulators are permitted; no probability or coverage result is included.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RestartDrawProbeAbort.lean#L26-L31

